# EarthIQ Core — Cline Rules

This repository is **EarthIQ Core**, a "pluggable monolith" geo-platform. A core
FastAPI backend + React/Vite frontend are the always-present shell, and a set of
swappable **modules** (AI, hydrology, resources, urban-planning, notifications)
are mounted into it at build/wire time. This file is the source of truth for how
to work in this repo. Follow it.

---

## 1. Non-negotiable rules (read first)

1. **Donot use setup-cli venv for environment. Use Docker / Docker Compose to run and test. Do NOT create or use a
   `venv` for this project.** The backend and frontend are consumed as
   long-running Compose services (`backend`, `frontend`) plus their support
   services (`db`, `redis`, `rustfs`). All code changes are verified by
   restarting / re-running the Compose services, not by local interpreter
   shells. (Local `pytest` for module backend tests _is_ allowed — see §6 —
   because it runs hermetically against in-memory SQLite with no real DB and no
   `venv`; it must not spin up a venv.)
2. **Modules are accessed through the services, never standalone.** To exercise
   a module, run it inside the `backend` and/or `frontend` Compose services.
   Do not add a separate "run this module in isolation" workflow that bypasses
   the service wiring.
3. **Frontend: reuse `@packages/ui` components BEFORE creating new ones.** The
   design-system package (`frontend/packages/ui`) already ships Button, Input,
   Select, Modal, Drawer, Dropdown, Toast, Card, Tabs, Sidebar, Badge, Checkbox,
   Switch, Slider, Pagination, Skeleton, Spinner, Alert, EmptyState, Command
   Palette, Tooltip, and more (see §5.3). Only create a new component when
   `@packages/ui` genuinely lacks the capability, and then prefer adding it to
   `@packages/ui` over inlining it in `apps/web` so it stays reusable.
4. **Styling lives in `frontend/apps/web/src/styles/globals.css`.** Do not scatter
   ad-hoc CSS files. Use the design tokens (CSS variables) and utility classes
   defined there (see §5.4). Tailwind v4 is available as a fallback but the
   token system is the primary mechanism.
5. **Do NOT hand-edit generated files.** These are produced by `setup sync` /
   the setup CLI and will be overwritten:
   - `frontend/apps/web/src/module-registry.generated.ts`
   - `frontend/apps/web/src/modules.generated.ts` (tombstone)
   - `frontend/apps/web/modules.paths.json`
   - `frontend/apps/web/tsconfig.paths.json`
   - `docker-compose.yaml` (root)
   - `backend/alembic.ini`
   - `frontend/apps/web/package.json` `@modules/*` dependency entries
     Change the _source_ (`modules.registry.yaml`, each module's `module.yaml`,
     `modules.lock.yaml`) and re-run the setup CLI.

