## 2. Project structure (overview / guide)

```
core/                                  # repository root (CWD)
├── .clinerules                        # THIS FILE — AI/agent working rules
├── README.md
├── LICENSE.txt
├── modules.registry.yaml              # CATALOG of available modules (name, version, repo)
├── modules.lock.yaml                  # GENERATED/selected modules actually installed
├── .env                               # shared env for all services (gitignored; source of APP_ENV)
│
├── backend/                           # CORE backend (always present)
│   ├── pyproject.toml                 # FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Alembic + deps (uv-managed)
│   ├── uv.lock
│   ├── alembic.ini.tpl                # committed Alembic template (generated alembic.ini is gitignored)
│   ├── alembic/                       # core migrations (versions/*.py)
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py                    # FastAPI app: lifespan, CORS, core routers, load_modules()
│   │   ├── module_loader.py           # mounts module routers from modules.lock.yaml at startup
│   │   ├── core/                      # config.py (Settings), db.py (Base/engine/get_db), security.py, storage.py
│   │   └── api/                       # core domain routers: auth, data, maps, projects, viz,
│   │        │                          storage, collab, modules, maps/share
│   │        └── <domain>/            # each = {router.py, models.py, schemas.py, service.py}
│   └── tests/                         # core pytest suite (in-memory SQLite, ASGITransport)
│
├── frontend/                          # pnpm monorepo (root package.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml)
│   ├── apps/
│   │   └── web/                       # THE shell app (Vite + React 19)
│   │       ├── package.json           # depends on @packages/ui, charts, cookie-consent (+ generated @modules/*)
│   │       ├── vite.config.ts
│   │       ├── tsconfig.json          # extends generated tsconfig.paths.json
│   │       ├── modules.paths.json     # GENERATED: @modules/* → ../modules/<name>/frontend/src/index.ts
│   │       ├── tsconfig.paths.json    # GENERATED: TS paths for @modules/*
│   │       └── src/
│   │           ├── App.tsx            # shell: dynamic module routing (never names a module directly)
│   │           ├── main.tsx
│   │           ├── module-registry.generated.ts  # GENERATED lazy registry
│   │           ├── pages/             # core pages: Dashboard, Map, Data, Projects, Admin, Public, ...
│   │           ├── components/        # app-level (data/, map/, ProtectedRoute, AppShell, ...)
│   │           ├── hooks/             # useMapLibre, etc.
│   │           ├── lib/               # auth, theme, modules (useModules)
│   │           └── styles/globals.css # DESIGN TOKENS + utility classes (SINGLE STYLE SOURCE)
│   └── packages/                      # shared workspace packages (design system + libs)
│       ├── ui/                        # @packages/ui  — DESIGN SYSTEM (components, hooks, contexts, utils)
│       ├── charts/                    # @packages/charts
│       ├── cookie-consent/            # @packages/cookie-consent
│       ├── map/                       # @packages/map (MapLibre helpers)
│       ├── language/ onboarding/ accessibility/
│       └── eslint-config/ prettier-config/ typescript-config/  (tooling)
│
├── modules/                           # pluggable feature modules (gitignored clones / local dev)
│   └── <name>-module/                 # e.g. notification-module, ai-module, resources-module
│       ├── module.yaml                # MODULE MANIFEST (backend + frontend + infra + capabilities)
│       ├── backend/
│       │   ├── pyproject.toml         # module runtime deps (installed by backend Dockerfile)
│       │   ├── module_<pkg>/          # package: router, service, schemas, models, db, ...
│       │   ├── alembic/               # OPTIONAL module migrations (merged into core alembic.ini)
│       │   └── tests/                 # hermetic pytest suite (in-memory SQLite)
│       ├── frontend/
│       │   ├── package.json           # @modules/<name> workspace package
│       │   └── src/index.ts           # MUST export: Page, routePath, navItem (+ optional clients)
│       └── infra/
│           └── compose.module.yaml    # OPTIONAL extra services/volumes (merged into root compose)
│
├── infra/
│   ├── docker/
│   │   ├── docker-compose.base.yaml   # db, redis, rustfs, backend, frontend (the source compose)
│   │   ├── backend.dev.Dockerfile     # uv + system site-packages + module deps + hot reload
│   │   ├── backend.prod.Dockerfile
│   │   ├── frontend.dev.Dockerfile    # pnpm install + build, runs `pnpm --filter web dev`
│   │   ├── frontend.prod.Dockerfile
│   │   ├── nginx.conf                 # prod reverse proxy
│   │   └── postgres.Dockerfile
│   └── scripts/start.sh               # prod uvicorn launcher
│
├── setup/                             # the "pluggable-monolith" CLI (`setup` command)
│   └── src/setup_cli/
│       ├── cli.py                     # init / add / remove / update / list / sync
│       ├── registry.py                # ROOT, load_registry/lock, load_module_meta
│       ├── installer.py               # clone/clone_module/install_selected/remove_module
│       ├── workspace.py               # writes backend alembic.ini + frontend paths/tsconfig
│       ├── codegen.py                 # generates module-registry.generated.ts
│       └── compose.py                 # generates root docker-compose.yaml (dev/prod)
│
└── docs/                              # test_plan.md, etc.
```

### How the pieces fit together

- `setup` CLI reads `modules.registry.yaml` → installs (clones) the selected
  modules into `modules/`, records them in `modules.lock.yaml`, then re-wires:
  backend Alembic migrations, frontend path aliases, the lazy module registry,
  and the root `docker-compose.yaml`. Run `setup sync` after editing any
  module's `module.yaml` to re-generate all of that.
- At backend startup, `app.module_loader.load_modules(app)` iterates
  `modules.lock.yaml → selected`, reads each `module.yaml`, injects the module
  `backend/` dir onto `sys.path`, imports its ORM models (so `Base.metadata`
  is populated), then imports and mounts its router under
  `"/api" + backend.prefix`.
- The frontend shell (`App.tsx`) fetches `/api/modules`, intersects enabled
  modules with the generated `moduleRegistry`, lazy-imports each bundle, and
  mounts `<Route path={routePath} element={<Page/>}>` plus the nav item. The
  shell never hard-codes a module name.

---

## 3. Docker & Compose workflow (REQUIRED)

The canonical stack is defined in `infra/docker/docker-compose.base.yaml` and
materialized as root `docker-compose.yaml` by `setup sync` (`compose.py`).
`APP_ENV` in `.env` selects dev vs prod wiring:

- **dev** (default): uses `*.dev.Dockerfile`s, bind-mounts `backend/`,
  `frontend/`, `modules/`, and `modules.lock.yaml` into the containers, so edits
  hot-reload. Ports: frontend `:3000`, backend `:8000`.
- **prod**: uses `*.prod.Dockerfile`s, strips dev bind mounts (code baked into
  the image), frontend served by nginx on `:80`.

### Services & ports

| Service    | Purpose                             | Host port  | Internal access (from `backend`) |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------- |
| `db`       | PostgreSQL (PostGIS)                | 5432       | `db:5432`                        |
| `redis`    | Redis 7                             | 6379       | `redis:6379`                     |
| `rustfs`   | S3-compatible object store (RustFS) | 9000/9001  | `rustfs:9000`                    |
| `backend`  | FastAPI (uvicorn)                   | 8000       | `backend:8000`                   |
| `frontend` | Vite dev server / nginx (prod)      | 3000 (dev) | `frontend:3000`                  |

Inside the Compose network services reach each other **by name**, not
`localhost`. The base compose overrides `DATABASE_URL` and `STORAGE_ENDPOINT`
with the service names; real env vars win over the `.env` file.

### Everyday commands (run from the repo root)

```bash
# Generate / regenerate the root docker-compose.yaml (after any module or
# module.yaml change) — dev mode:
APP_ENV=dev python -m setup_cli.cli sync          # or: setup sync (if installed)

# Full bring-up (build + start detached):
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml up --build -d

# Watch logs:
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml logs -f backend
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml logs -f frontend

# Rebuild a single service after code edits (dev bind-mounts usually just reload):
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml restart backend
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml up --build -d backend frontend

# Tear down (keep volumes by default; drop data with -v):
docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml down
```

`setup init` does the whole install + `up --build -d` in one shot and prints the
URL (http://localhost:3000).

### Access the APIs (for testing)

- Backend health: `curl http://localhost:8000/api/health`
- OpenAPI docs: `http://localhost:8000/api/docs`
- Auth flow: `POST /api/auth/register` → `POST /api/auth/token` → `GET /api/auth/me`
  (Bearer `access_token` on subsequent calls; password min policy enforced).
- Core modules API: `GET /api/modules` (list + enabled flag) — the frontend
  shell uses this to decide which module routes to mount.
- Example module API: `GET/POST /api/notifications` (notification-module),
  `GET /api/resources` (resources-module), etc. — mounted under the module's
  `backend.prefix`.
- Frontend: `http://localhost:3000` (dev) / `http://localhost:80` (prod).

### Adding a new module to the stack

1. Ensure the module is listed in `modules.registry.yaml` (name, version, repo
   or a `file://` local path for local development) and cloned into
   `modules/<name>-module/` (via `setup add <name>` or manually).
2. Fill in `modules/<name>-module/module.yaml` (see §4 contract).
3. Run `setup sync` → regenerates `docker-compose.yaml`, frontend paths,
   module registry, and (if the module has `alembic/versions/`) core
   `alembic.ini`.
4. `docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml up --build -d` and hit the module's
   `/api/<prefix>` endpoint to verify.

---

## 4. Module contract

### `module.yaml` (per module) — the manifest the loader + CLI read

```yaml
name: notification-module
version: "0.1.0"
description: "..."
backend:
  package: module_notifications # importable python package name
  router_attr: "router:router" # "<module>:<attr>" → module router
  models_attr: "models" # optional; imported at startup for Base.metadata
  prefix: /notifications # mounted at /api/notifications
frontend:
  package_name: "@modules/notifications"
  entry: "src/index.ts"
infra:
  compose_file: infra/compose.module.yaml # optional extra services/volumes
  env: []
capabilities:
  - in-app-notifications
  - real-time
depends_on: []
```

### Module backend conventions

- Package layout: `backend/module_<pkg>/` with `router.py`, `service.py`,
  `schemas.py`, `models.py`, and a thin `db.py` that **re-exports core
  `Base` / `AsyncSessionLocal` / `get_db` from `app.core.db`** (do not build
  your own engine). The module builds on the core runtime (FastAPI /
  SQLAlchemy / Pydantic) — it is mounted into the _same_ process, so
  `app.*` is always importable at runtime.
- `router.py`: create `router = APIRouter()`; declare endpoints with
  `response_model=` and `tags=[<module>]`. Reuse the core auth dependency
  (`from app.api.auth.router import get_current_user`) as the single source of
  truth for the current user; use `_require_admin` pattern for superuser-only
  routes. Keep business logic in `service.py` (router → service → db).
- `schemas.py`: Pydantic request/response models; use `*.model_dump(mode="json")`
  when serializing across the wire.
- `models.py`: SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM models on the shared `Base`. If you add
  tables, provide an Alembic migration under the module's `alembic/versions/`
  (they are auto-merged into core `alembic.ini` by `setup sync`), and keep the
  module test harness able to `Base.metadata.create_all`.
- Optional cross-cutting capability: expose a programmatic helper
  (e.g. `module_notifications.router.emit(...)`) other modules can call.

### Module frontend conventions

- `frontend/src/index.ts` MUST export exactly:
  - `Page` (a default-exported React component) — the module's root page
  - `routePath: string` — e.g. `"/resources"` (no trailing slash)
  - `navItem: { label: string; to: string; icon?: string }`
  - (optionally) an API client, types, and sub-components the shell may import.
- The module `frontend/package.json` name must match `frontend.package_name`
  in `module.yaml` (e.g. `@modules/notifications`).
- Build module UI **on top of `@packages/ui`** (see §5.3) and the core
  `globals.css` tokens (see §5.4).

---

## 5. Frontend conventions

### 5.1 Stack

- pnpm workspace monorepo (`frontend/package.json`, `packageManager:
pnpm@9.15.0`). Apps: `apps/web`. Packages: `packages/*`. Modules' frontends
  join the workspace via the `../modules/*/frontend` glob in
  `pnpm-workspace.yaml`.
- `apps/web`: Vite 8 + React 19 + TypeScript 6, `react-router-dom` v7,
  `@tanstack/react-query`, `zustand`, `maplibre-gl`, `lucide-react`.
- Common commands (run in `frontend/`, or inside the `frontend` Compose
  service):
  ```bash
  pnpm --filter web dev      # dev server (this is what the frontend service runs)
  pnpm --filter web build    # production build
  pnpm --filter web lint     # eslint
  pnpm lint                  # across all packages
  ```
  The frontend Compose service runs `pnpm --filter web dev`; after editing
  frontend code, either rely on Vite HMR or `docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml
restart frontend`.

### 5.2 Aliases

- `@/*` → `apps/web/src/*`.
- `@modules/<name>` → `../modules/<name>-module/frontend/src/index.ts` (generated
  into `modules.paths.json` + `tsconfig.paths.json`). Never import a module by
  a raw relative path; use the `@modules/*` alias or the shell's lazy registry.

### 5.3 Prefer `@packages/ui` components (RULE)

Import from the package root: `import { Button, Input, Modal, ... } from
"@packages/ui";` (re-exports components, contexts, hooks, `cn`, types).
CATEGORIES AVAILABLE (create a new component only if one of these is missing):

- **primitives:** Button, ButtonGroup, IconButton, Input, Textarea, Select,
  Checkbox, Radio, Slider, Switch, Text, Badge
- **form:** Form, FormField, DatePicker, TimePicker, FileUpload, Rating
- **layout:** Card, Container, Divider, Grid, Stack
- **navigation:** Navbar, Sidebar, Breadcrumb, Tabs, Stepper, Pagination
- **overlay:** Modal, Drawer, Dropdown, Popover, Tooltip, ConfirmDialog,
  CommandPalette
- **data-display:** Accordion, Avatar, CodeBlock, Kbd, Stat, Table, Timeline
- **feedback:** Alert, Banner, EmptyState, ErrorBoundary (+ `withErrorBoundary`,
  `useErrorBoundary`), Progress, Skeleton, Spinner
- **interaction:** DragAndDrop suite (`DndProvider`, `Draggable`, `Droppable`,
  `SortableList`, `FileDropZone`, `useDragAndDrop`, ...)
- **common:** OptimizedImage, ThemeToogle
- **contexts:** `ThemeProvider` / `useTheme`, `ToastProvider` / `useToast`
- **hooks:** `useClickOutside`, `useKeyboard`/`useEscapeKey`, `useDisclosure`,
  `useCopyToClipboard`, `useMediaQuery`/`useIsMobile/Tablet/Desktop`,
  `useOnScreen`, `useDebounce`/`useDebouncedCallback`, `useLocalStorage`,
  `usePrevious`, `useLockBodyScroll`, `usePerformance`
- **utils:** `cn` (class merge), `security`, `variants`, `webVitals`

When you need something not listed, add it to `frontend/packages/ui` (new
`components/<category>/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` + re-export from the category
`components/index.ts` and the package `src/index.ts`) rather than forking it in
`apps/web` or a module.

### 5.4 Styling — `src/styles/globals.css` (RULE)

The **single source of design tokens** is
`frontend/apps/web/src/styles/globals.css`. It defines:

- **CSS custom properties** (use these, not raw hex/oklch):
  - brand: `--primary`, `--primary-dark/-light/-hover`, `--secondary`,
    `--accent`, and `*-dark/-light` variants
  - surfaces: `--bg-primary/-secondary/-tertiary/-elevated`, `--surface`,
    `--surface-hover/-active`
  - text: `--text-primary/-secondary/-tertiary/-inverse/-on-primary`
  - borders: `--border-primary/-secondary/-hover/-focus`
  - status: `--success/-warning/-error/-info` (each with `-bg/-text/-border`)
  - interactive: `--input-bg/-border/-focus-border/-placeholder`,
    `--toggle-*`, `--button-disabled-*`
  - elevation: `--shadow-xs…2xl`, `--shadow-inner`, `--shadow-primary`
  - misc: `--overlay(-light)`, `--backdrop`, `--divider`, `--ring(-offset)`,
    `--radius-sm…full`, `--transition-fast/normal/slow/slower`,
    `--z-dropdown/sticky/fixed/modal/popover/tooltip/toast`, scrollbar vars
- **Ready utility classes** (reuse, don't redefine): `.card`, `.card-elevated`,
  `.btn` (+ `.btn-primary/-secondary/-ghost`), `.input`, `.badge`
  (+ `.badge-primary/-success/-warning/-error/-info`), `.toggle`, `.skeleton`,
  `.overlay`, `.overlay-light`, `.divider`, `.text-gradient(-accent/-secondary)`,
  `.bg-base/.bg-surface/.bg-elevated`, `.text-base/.text-muted/.text-subtle`,
  `.border-base/.border-subtle`, `.shadow-base/.shadow-elevated`,
  `.bg-success-subtle/...`, safe-area `.pb-safe/.pt-safe/.px-safe`, and the
  `.animate-*` animation helpers (`animate-fade-in`, `animate-scale-in`,
  `animate-slide-up`, `animate-spin`, `animate-pulse`, `animate-shake`, ...).
- **Dark mode** is a `.dark` class on the root (driven by the UI
  `ThemeProvider`); every token has a dark override under `:root.dark`. Don't
  write separate dark CSS — just use the tokens.
- Tailwind v4 is imported (`@import "tailwindcss"`) and `@source
"../../../../packages"` is set so package code is scanned; use utilities for
  layout/spacing, but prefer the token variables and the classes above for
  colors, radii, shadows, and interactive states.

### 5.5 Shell rules

- `App.tsx` is the shell. Do NOT add module-specific routes/imports to it;
  module routing flows through `module-registry.generated.ts` + `/api/modules`.
- Put core pages in `src/pages/`, core shared components in
  `src/components/`, data hooks in `src/hooks/`, and API/auth/theme/module
  helpers in `src/lib/`.

---

## 6. Testing

- **Backend (core + every module) uses hermetic pytest** — no venv, no real DB,
  no network:
  - In-memory SQLite via `sqlite+aiosqlite` + `StaticPool` (shared single
    in-memory DB), `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`.
  - FastAPI app driven through `httpx.AsyncClient` + `ASGITransport` (skips
    ASGI lifespan).
  - `app.dependency_overrides[get_db]` swaps the session.
  - `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio` with `asyncio_mode = "auto"`.
  - A `conftest.py` builds a small test app (auth + the module router), creates
    tables from `Base.metadata.create_all`, rolls back per test, and offers
    `admin` / `user_a` / `user_b` fixtures (register → token → user_id).
- Run module tests (from the module's `backend/` dir; uses a venv-free
  hermetic harness, not a project venv):
  ```bash
  cd modules/<name>-module/backend && python -m pytest -ra
  ```
  Core tests:
  ```bash
  cd backend && python -m pytest -ra
  ```
- Integration tests that need a real PostGIS DB are marked `@pytest.mark.
integration` and are run against the `db` Compose service — they are the only
  tests that touch real infra.
- For UI changes, verify through the running `frontend` Compose service
  (http://localhost:3000) — typically with the browser tool — rather than a
  separate local dev server.

---

## 7. Definition of Done (per task)

- [ ] Code change respects the module boundaries and conventions above.
- [ ] No `venv` was created; work was verified via the Compose services
      (or hermetic `pytest` for backend logic).
- [ ] `setup sync` was run if any `module.yaml` / registry / lock changed;
      generated files were not hand-edited.
- [ ] New/reused UI uses `@packages/ui` + `globals.css` tokens; no stray CSS
      files.
- [ ] `docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml up --build -d` succeeds and the
      affected endpoint/page works (health check / browser verification).
